A change of packages/fcl-passrc/src/pasresolver.pp of Free Pascal 3.2.2 (tag release_3_2_2), applied by get.sh.
Licence of this patch: that of the patched file, the LGPL with the static linking exception of Free Pascal (COPYING.FPC
in the FPC sources); see README.md.

1. TPasResolver.CheckUseAsType: in ObjFPC the bare name of a generic is allowed inside the implementation of its own
   methods too (class function TOwned.Own(AObj: T): TOwned), as FPC allows it.
2. The for-in enumerator may be a record, as FPC allows (for V in Ch over TChan<T>).
3. A class operator of a record is not static, and its implementation is found by the operator name.
4. ObjFPC passes a typed pointer to a var or out argument of type Pointer (GetMem(P, Size)), as FPC does.
5. A pointer to a member type of a generic declared after it (PData = ^TData) is specialized once all members are.
6. InterfaceOnly (a used unit read up to its implementation): no section, method bodies or generic bodies are required.

